      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I need some help putting together a minute-by-minute logistics timeline for the opening ceremony of our medical symposium in Geneva next month. It's a 3-day event. For the opening ceremony on Day 1, I need to account for: speaker arrivals, AV/tech setup and testing, catering staff getting the coffee/pastry station ready, and the actual keynote starting. Can you draft a schedule for the first two hours of the morning?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, here's your outline for the first two hours of the opening ceremony:\n\n09:00 - 09:30 AM: Door of the hall opens, guests begin arriving, and a welcome speech is given.\n\n09:30 - 09:40 AM: Registration and badges are collected for the attendees.\n\n09:40 - 09:50 AM: Speaker arrivals begin; registration desk staff provides guidance as speakers check in.\n\n09:50 - 10:00 AM: Waitstaff from the catering team position themselves at tables to start serving coffee and pastries.\n\n10:00 - 10:05 AM: Tech team arrives on-site; the AV setup begins.\n\n10:05 - 10:20 AM: Lead technician conducts final checks on microphones, speakers, screens, and cameras.\n\n10:20 - 10:30 AM: Simultaneous testing of audio, video, and lighting systems is performed.\n\n10:30 - 10:45 AM: AV/tech setup re-testing and technician confirmations.\n\n10:45 - 11:00 AM: In case of technical glitches, the speaker is provided with a microphone and integrated into the setup smoothly.\n\n11:00 - 11:05 AM: Official commencement of the keynote speech.",
